Package: offtake
Title: Sustainability Indices and Models for Wildlife Harvest and Hunting
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Stanislas",
           family = "Gandaho",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "stangandaho@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-4969-1252"))
Description: Toolkit for assessing the sustainability of
    wildlife exploitation (bushmeat hunting, recreational hunting and
    fisheries). It implements the main index-based and model-based approaches
    catalogued by Adounke et al. (2026) <doi:10.1016/j.biocon.2025.111606>
    and reviewed by Weinbaum et al. (2013) <doi:10.1111/ele.12008>. Indices
    compare a harvest or abundance metric between hunted and reference sites:
    age structure comparison ('asc'), hunting yield comparison ('hyco') and
    population density comparison ('pdc'). Models compare observed offtake with
    an estimated maximum sustainable harvest: the production model of Robinson
    and Redford (1991) ('pro'), potential
    biological removal of Wade (1998) <doi:10.1111/j.1748-7692.1998.tb00688.x>
    ('pbr'), the maximum sustainable yield of the logistic model ('msy'), the
    spatially explicit source-sink model of Levi et al. (2009)
    ('biode') and a stochastic
    extension of PBR in the spirit of Manlik et al. (2022)
    <doi:10.1111/cobi.13897> ('samse').
